    "grid": {
      "width": 150,
      "height": 150,
      "depth": 150
    },
    "prior": {
      "axis": [
        0.55528,
        0.831663,
        0
      ],
      "center": [
        74.5,
        74.5,
        74.5
      ],
      "binWidth": 1
    },
    "tau": 0.001,
    "iterations": 100,
    "blackLevel": [
      0.02,
      0.02,
      0.016
    ],
    "displayExposure": 1.5,
    "slices": 48,
    "assumptions": [
      "Depth follows the deprojected density (Prugniel & Simien 1997) of Kormendy et al.'s (2009) Table 1 major-axis Sérsic fit to NGC 4406: n = 10.27 (+0.49, -0.35), half-light radius 2341.62 (+625, -357) arcsec, on an oblate spheroid whose axis is M86's minor axis (position angle 213.73000000000002 degrees: the major axis is at 123.73 degrees in the last row of Table 3, at 799.834 arcsec, because the fit's half-light radius lies beyond the measured profile) in the plane of the sky, axis ratio 0.625 (1 - 0.375, the ellipticity of the same row). The survey image's light along each sight line is kept; only its depth comes from the prior. The intrinsic orientation is not measured.",
      "The prior ends at 0.342 half-light radii, where Kormendy et al.'s Table 3 profile of NGC 4406 stops (799.834 arcsec, 66.2 kpc at 17.1 Mpc); light beyond that spheroid is not drawn.",
      "The 3000 x 3000 px cutout is requested on M86's HyperLEDA position (PGC 40653: 186.549081, +12.94581) in a tangent projection, north up and east left, 0.444352 degrees wide (twice 799.834 arcsec, 0.5332 arcsec per px), so its registration is the request's.",
      "NOX removes stars; what it leaves is masked afterwards: 36 neighbouring galaxies from HyperLEDA PGC (Paturel et al. 2003, CDS VII/237: every galaxy with a D25 whose mask reaches the cutout) at 3 times their D25 radius, M87's rule; 16 from the 2MASS Extended Source Catalog (CDS VII/233), which sizes the galaxies HyperLEDA gives no D25, at 3 times their K-band 20 mag isophotal radius; and the 24 Gaia DR3 stars brighter than G = 15, whose haloes NOX leaves, at 45 arcsec for G = 11, scaled with brightness (a factor 10 in radius per 5 magnitudes). No mask reaches beyond nine tenths of its distance from M86's centre (chosen here), so every isophote keeps unmasked light. A masked pixel takes the median of the unmasked light on its own isophote (the ellipse through it with the measured axis ratio and position angle), never more than it held.",
      "Every pixel is clamped to the median of the 51 px square around it, so star haloes and small background galaxies that NOX and the masks leave are not spread through the spheroid.",
      "Black level per channel: the median of the cleaned cutout's four 150 px corners, red 0.020, green 0.020, blue 0.016 (5, 5 and 4 of 255).",
      "The color is the survey's published g, r, i display composite, not calibrated photometry. Single-image depth is modelled by the prior, not measured."
    ],
    "compactClamp": {
      "windowPx": 51,
      "basis": "51 px (27.2 arcsec, 2.2 kpc) is about two and a half of the grid's 20.0 px cells, the proportion M87's recipe uses: light more compact than that cannot be M86's smooth light at this grid."
    },
    "shapePrior": {
      "components": [
